# Copy to .env.development (gitignored via .env.*) for local Vite HTTPS same-origin entry.
#
# Browser traffic must use the Vite origin only. API calls use the relative `/api`
# proxy (see vite.config.ts); do not point the browser at a direct API origin in
# local auth development (Secure cookie + CSRF require same-origin HTTPS).

# Public SPA origin (must match AUTH_BROWSER_ORIGINS on the API Service).
VITE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://127.0.0.1:5173

# Prefer relative same-origin `/api` (empty or unset). Absolute API URLs are
# reserved for non-browser tooling and must not be used by the SPA auth client.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Legacy registration shell default (HTTP direct). Phone-auth flows must not rely
# on this once HTTPS same-origin proxy is active.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
